<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Duchy of Prussia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1525–1701</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Ducal Prussia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> was the state created in 1525 when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-duke-of-prussia">Albert of Brandenburg-Ansbach</a>, the last Grand Master in Prussia, secularised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a>'s lands and became their hereditary duke under Polish overlordship. It was the first state to adopt <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lutheranism">Lutheranism</a> officially. Inherited by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> in 1618 and freed from Polish suzerainty in 1657, it became the Kingdom of Prussia in 1701.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/duchy-of-prussia.jpg" alt="Duchy of Prussia" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Orange Tuesday · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Ducal_Prussia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
